  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read from the code",
      "items": [
        "The SPL checks sml, trustos and lk against a key fingerprint it carries",
        "One check fails: it tries the backup copy. That fails too: an endless loop",
        "lk asks the secure world (command 0x33) if the miscdata unlock record is genuine",
        "That gives locked or unlocked",
        "Unlocked: the secure-world check of boot/recovery is skipped, state 2 (orange)",
        "Locked: lk sends the image with command 0x20. Result 0 is state 0 (green), 5 is state 1 (yellow), anything else state 3 (red)",
        "Locked and not booting recovery: vbmeta_system is checked the same way",
        "Reply does not match the call's return: lk logs tos return error! and loops forever",
        "lk always runs its own libavb too; its result is logged and feeds the kernel command line, it does not set the state",
        "Green or yellow: lk logs a line and carries on booting",
        "Orange: a wait of up to 10000 ticks, then it carries on booting",
        "Red: a message on screen, then Download Mode (Odin), and it stays there",
        "Android gets androidboot.verifiedbootstate=green|yellow|orange|red (green for any unknown number)",
        "Beside it: androidboot.flash.locked=0|1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Seen on the tablets",
      "items": [
        "After unlocking, on both real tablets: flash.locked 0, verifiedbootstate orange",
        "LineageOS boots"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not read",
      "items": [
        "What trusts the first loader (SPL) itself",
        "What the orange step shows on screen: the unlocked warning is most likely this step, but its three calls were not read",
        "What sits behind lk's own key-trust check",
        "Which images besides boot and recovery go through the loader path"
      ]
    }
  ]
